{{fbdoc item="title" value="IMPORT"}}----
External linkage attribute for public data located in DLL's

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	[[KeyPgExtern|Extern]] **Import** //symbolname//[( //subscripts//)] [ [[KeyPgAlias|alias]] "//aliasname//"] [ [[KeyPgAs|as]] [[DataType|DataType]]] [, ...]
##
{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	Is used only (with the ##[[KeyPgExtern|Extern]]## keyword) in external modules to access global variables from 32-bit and 64-bit Windows DLLs: the variable names will be added to the dynamic library import list so that their addresses can be fixed at run-time.
	This is due to the level of indirection on any such access: an implicit pointer dereference.
	The declaration must match the DLL's C data type. A C ##int## is 32 bits on both Windows targets, so use FreeBASIC ##Long##. FreeBASIC ##Integer## is native-sized and is 64 bits on Win64.
	The import library and DLL must match the application's target architecture. Win32 and Win64 use different import-address symbol prefixes, which the compiler supplies automatically.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/module/mydll.c"}}%%(c)
/*
    Project: FreeBASIC manual examples
    ----------------------------------

    File: examples/manual/module/mydll.c

    Purpose:

        Provide the C DLL used by the manual's IMPORT example.

    Responsibilities:

        - export one integer data symbol from a Windows DLL

    This file intentionally does NOT contain:

        - executable startup code
        - FreeBASIC declarations for importing the symbol

    See also:

        https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=KeyPgImport
*/

/* mydll.c :
	compile with
	  gcc -shared -Wl,--strip-all -Wl,--out-implib,libmydll.dll.a -o mydll.dll mydll.c
*/
__declspec( dllexport ) int MyDll_Data = 0x1234;

/* end of examples/manual/module/mydll.c */
%%

{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/module/import.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/module/import.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'IMPORT'
'' Purpose: Read a C DLL's exported 32-bit integer.
'' Responsibilities: DLL import linkage and matching the C data width.
'' This example contains no DLL implementation or runtime loading code.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=KeyPgImport
'' --------

/'  import.bas :
	Compile with
	  fbc import.bas
'/
#inclib "mydll"

'' C int remains 32 bits on both Win32 and Win64.
Extern Import MyDll_Data Alias "MyDll_Data" As Long

Print "&h" + Hex( MyDll_Data )

' Output:
' &h1234

'' end of import.bas
%%


{{fbdoc item="lang"}}
	- Not available in the //[[CompilerOptlang|-lang qb]]// dialect unless referenced with the alias ##**""__Import""**##.

{{fbdoc item="diff"}}
	- New to ""FreeBASIC""

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- ##[[KeyPgExtern|Extern]]##

